// e-prop training of a recurrent spiking network (examples/snn_train) on
// its toy task: A then B or B then A. It learns (the loss falls, the test
// samples it never learned from come out right), and it says to the bit
// what the same network trained in plain C says (check/toy.c, the same
// numbers at random, the same order of every sum, the same Adam): every
// loss, every count, and a checksum of the bits of every weight. On one
// thread and on many alike.
// RUN: %ent run %S/../../examples/snn_train/toy.ent > %t.one
// RUN: env ENT_PARALLEL_MIN=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=8 %ent run --parallel %S/../../examples/snn_train/toy.ent > %t.all
// RUN: clang -O2 -ffp-contract=off %S/../../examples/snn_train/check/toy.c -lm -o %t.c
// RUN: %t.c > %t.ref
// RUN: diff %t.ref %t.one
// RUN: diff %t.ref %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s < %t.one
//
// Backpropagation through time on the same task (toy_bptt.ent), on one
// thread and on many alike.
// RUN: %ent run %S/../../examples/snn_train/toy_bptt.ent > %t.bptt.one
// RUN: env ENT_PARALLEL_MIN=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=8 %ent run --parallel %S/../../examples/snn_train/toy_bptt.ent > %t.bptt.all
// RUN: diff %t.bptt.one %t.bptt.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BPTT < %t.bptt.one
//
// Its gradient with the recurrent term left out is e-prop's, added in
// another order: within a millionth of the largest, for the synapses and
// for the readouts' weights and biases. With the term in, the synapses'
// differ (by a third); the readouts' are the same still.
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples/snn_train %S/../../examples/snn_train/check/same_gradient.ent \
// RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SAME

// CHECK: epoch 1 loss 0.362811 train 184/200 test 200/200
// CHECK: epoch 3 loss 0.005185 train 200/200 test 200/200
// CHECK: epoch 30 loss 0.000053 train 200/200 test 200/200
// CHECK: weights 74942124909

// BPTT: epoch 1 loss 0.34394 train 184/200 test 200/200
// BPTT: epoch 30 loss 0.000016 train 200/200 test 200/200
// BPTT: weights 77113250418

// SAME-COUNT-4: through 0.0: synapses {{[0-9.]+}}, differ 0.{{[0-9]+}} millionths; readouts {{[0-9.]+}}, differ 0.{{[0-9]+}} millionths
// SAME-COUNT-4: through 1.0: synapses {{[0-9.]+}}, differ {{[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]+}}.{{[0-9]+}} millionths; readouts {{[0-9.]+}}, differ 0.{{[0-9]+}} millionths
